# 23. ROW LEVEL SECURITY AND SECURITY

This is a critical part of the application.

Enable RLS on every table containing user data.

Define policies for:

- Profiles.
- Likes.
- Matches.
- Messages.
- Conversations.
- Secret admirer requests.
- Confessions.
- Comments.
- Couple spaces.
- Couple memories.
- Communities.
- Event registrations.
- Reports.
- Notifications.
- Administrative records.

Rules:

1. Users can edit only their own profiles.
2. Users can read only permitted profile fields.
3. Only verified eligible users can participate in dating.
4. Only matched users can access their conversations.
5. Only conversation members can access messages.
6. Only couple-space members can access their private couple content.
7. Only authorized moderators can access moderation queues.
8. Only administrators with suitable roles can perform administrative actions.
9. Users cannot approve their own verification.
10. Users cannot modify their own administrator roles.
11. Blocked users cannot contact the blocker.
12. Unmatched users cannot continue sending messages.
13. Notifications are visible only to their recipients.

Use server-side validation in addition to RLS.

Create automated tests for authorization boundaries.

Never trust client-supplied user IDs for privileged operations.

